From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dbghelp: CodeView records, data segments, handle data, memory scan and filter in minidumps

Crash reporters (Crashpad, .NET's dump writers, WER-style tools) ask
MiniDumpWriteDump for these; they were FIXMEs that wrote nothing:

- each PE module's CodeView record (the RSDS block naming the PDB, its
  GUID and age) is copied from the module's debug directory into the dump,
  so a debugger can find the symbols;
- MiniDumpWithDataSegs adds every module's writable, non-code sections to
  the memory list (modules whose callback keeps ModuleWriteDataSeg);
- MiniDumpWithHandleData writes the handle stream: each handle's value,
  type and object name, attributes, granted access and counts;
- MiniDumpScanMemory sets ModuleReferencedByMemory for modules that a
  value in a thread's stack points into, for the callback to decide;
- MiniDumpFilterMemory keeps, in the stacks, only the values a stack trace
  needs (addresses in modules or stacks); the rest are zeroed.

The module's PE layout is read whatever the target's bitness.

Wine's dbghelp minidump tests: no failures, as before (more of them run).

Gate: test/minidumpx-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_CV_RECORD, SG_MUTANT_NO_DATA_SEGS, SG_MUTANT_NO_HANDLE_DATA
(dbghelp/minidump.c).
---
--- a/dlls/dbghelp/minidump.c
+++ b/dlls/dbghelp/minidump.c
@@ -420,6 +420,142 @@ static  unsigned        dump_exception_info(struct dump_context* dc)
     return sizeof(mdExcpt);
